atlas CartPole bridge (atlas/bridge/cartpole_jaxued.py): train JaxUED's gymnax PLR script on the
ACL27 CartPole with ACL27's PPO settings. Every deviation from upstream (JaxUED 0f8f128); each new
option defaults to upstream behaviour, so upstream runs are unchanged:

src/jaxued/environments/gymnax/cartpole.py
  1. Level.init_range (default 0.05): reset draws each state component from U(-init_range,
     init_range); upstream hard-codes 0.05. ACL27's start spread is a task parameter.
  2. BOX + make_level_generator_box(): levels uniform in ACL27's box (length 0.25-1.5, masspole
     0.05-0.5, masscart 0.5-2.0, force_mag 4-16, init_range 0.05-0.3; acl_bench/envs/cartpole.py
     PARAM_BOUNDS), total_mass and polemass_length derived, gravity and tau at defaults.

examples/gymnax/gymnax_plr.py
  3. --env cartpole_acl27: CartPole with the box generator (eval levels stay upstream's).
  4. --acl27_mlp: ActorCriticMLP, acl_bench/ppo.py Agent's network (separate actor and critic,
     two 64-unit tanh layers each, orthogonal init sqrt(2) / 0.01 / 1.0), layers named after the
     torch state-dict entries. Upstream's feed-forward net has one hidden layer per branch.
  5. --no-clip_value: unclipped value loss (upstream clips it by clip_eps).
  6. --no-anneal_lr: constant learning rate (upstream anneals linearly to 0).
  7. --shuffle_samples: minibatches are random single steps of the rollout (feed-forward nets
     only); upstream's minibatches are whole per-env trajectories (here 2 of the 8 envs each).
  8. --params_out PATH: after training, saves the first repeat's params, the level buffer's
     scores/size/episode_count and the DR/replay update counts to an npz.

